<title>USA: Georgia Power sees 1,162 MW nuke back Sat.</title>
<headline>Georgia Power sees 1,162 MW nuke back Sat.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Georgia Power Co said Friday it expects its 1,162 megawatt (MW) Vogtle 2 nuclear unit, shut last month for a seasonal refueling outage, to be back in service on Saturday.</p>
<p>&quot;It is supposed to come back on line tomorrow,&quot; a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The Waynesboro, Ga., unit has been shut since September 8 and was scheduled to be off line until October 12.</p>
<p>Vogtle nuclear unit one, also 1,162 MWs, was running normally.</p>
<p>Georgia Power is a unit of Southern Co.</p>
<p>--J Silha, New York Power Desk 212-859-1624</p>
</text>
